    cortex-tools touched::tests::a_command_changed_what_its_look_found_and_not_the_workspace_it_declared
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_command_sends_the_turn_to_the_checks_by_what_its_look_found

[break] a-write-that-found-its-content-there-is-a-change
rule: A `write` or `edit` whose payload says `unchanged` changed nothing, and does not send its turn to the checks.
file: crates/cortex-tools/src/touched.rs
packages: cortex-tools, cortex-agent
in: changed_by
find: == Some("unchanged");
replace: == Some("never written");
caught-by:
    cortex-tools touched::tests::a_write_that_found_its_content_there_changed_nothing
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_write_that_found_its_content_there_does_not_send_the_turn_to_the_checks

[break] a-command-that-failed-changed-nothing
rule: A command that ran and failed has still changed what its look found: `sed -i … && make` that fails has edited.
file: crates/cortex-tools/src/touched.rs
packages: cortex-tools, cortex-agent
in: changed_by
find: ToolOutcome::Denied => Vec::new()
replace: ToolOutcome::Denied | ToolOutcome::Error => Vec::new()
caught-by:
    cortex-tools touched::tests::a_command_changed_what_its_look_found_and_not_the_workspace_it_declared
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_command_sends_the_turn_to_the_checks_by_what_its_look_found

[break] a-look-that-did-not-finish-is-no-change
rule: A look for what a command changed that did not finish means a change may have been made: the workspace stands for it.
file: crates/cortex-tools/src/touched.rs
packages: cortex-tools, cortex-agent
in: by_command
find: if !finished {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    cortex-tools touched::tests::a_command_changed_what_its_look_found_and_not_the_workspace_it_declared
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_command_sends_the_turn_to_the_checks_by_what_its_look_found

# --------------------------------------------------------- the stage

[break] a-round-runs-again-on-the-same-state
rule: A round of checks runs only when something changed since the last: the same checks on the same files say the same.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::verify
find: turn.changed = false;
replace: let _ = turn.changed;
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::after_a_failure_the_checks_run_again_only_when_something_changed

[break] a-round-starts-with-the-turns-time-spent
rule: No round starts once the turn's or the session's time limit is spent: the checks would run past it.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
find: && self.ledger.time_left() != Some(Duration::ZERO)
replace: && self.ledger.time_left() != Some(Duration::MAX)
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::no_round_starts_once_the_turns_time_is_spent

[break] a-round-is-not-told-the-time-left
rule: A round is told the time the turn's and the session's limits leave, so that no check runs past them.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::verify
find: deadline: self.ledger.time_left()
replace: deadline: None
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_round_is_told_its_place_and_the_time_the_turns_limits_leave

[break] an-interrupt-drops-the-round
rule: On an interrupt the loop waits for the round to stop what it runs, so that nothing of a check is left running and what it changed is recorded.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::verify
find: let outcome = self.verifier.verify(cx).await;
replace: let Some(outcome) = turn.cancel.race(self.verifier.verify(cx)).await else { return Phase::Interrupted(None); };
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::an_interrupt_waits_for_the_round_to_stop_what_it_runs

[break] a-check-that-stops-the-turn-completes-it
rule: A check that made the turn stop (a protected path changed, a process that could not be cleared) ends the turn `denied`, as a tool round the policy stopped does.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::verify
find: outcome: TurnOutcome::Denied
replace: outcome: TurnOutcome::Completed
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::a_check_that_stops_the_turn_ends_it_denied_and_the_model_is_told_why

[break] the-verdict-is-lost-with-the-turns-limit
rule: The verdict of the turn's checks is carried whenever a round ran, however the turn then ended: a failure is not lost when the turn runs out of time.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/turn.rs
in: Session::finish
find: (Some(verdict), _) => Some(verdict.clone())
replace: (Some(_), _) if end.outcome != TurnOutcome::Completed => None, (Some(verdict), _) => Some(verdict.clone())
caught-by:
    cortex-agent::it verifying::the_verdict_stays_with_a_turn_that_then_runs_out_of_time

# ---------------------------------------------------------- the settings

[break] a-project-turns-verification-up
rule: A project may turn verification down (`off` < `ask` < `auto`) and never up: up is the user's alone.
